      "note": "Codex reconciliation; PROVISIONAL machine alignment. Initial las/de'i/'bras bu attach to original karma/its/eventual consequences, not the earlier English virtue-and-result mentions; original, eventual and may be remain unwrapped. The established rang gi sde pa unit has provisional HGM Buddhist schools evidence; rang gi is not separately equated with Buddhist. Its sde pa member owns the first schools; the two repeated school nouns remain outside. sogs licenses and so on and requires a supplied-head allowlist entry. The temporal frame is a d3 recast of the entire interval before consequence-giving. In that giving event, karma is agent and consequence object, so 'byin pa owns gives. rtag par and 'gyur separately own unchanging and would have to be; rtag pas is kept whole, with causal force distributed beyond the adjective. don byed owns affecting; anything is English expansion. The final d2 includes the complete negative causal-relation clause: Tibetan says a consequence's arising FROM karma is untenable; English says one could never have a relation in which karma gives rise TO a consequence. The cause and result remain fixed. No atomic 'byung ba/gave rise claim or incomplete mi 'thad/could never have claim is banked. English rhetorical you remains outside. ni, la and other distributed framing are omitted without asserting absence."
